        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the inability to use immutable `FsPermission` objects as IPC parameters, which likely stemmed from the lack of a proper implementation for immutable permissions in the existing `FsPermission` class. The original implementation did not provide a way to create immutable instances that could be safely used in IPC, leading to potential issues when such objects were required.

        Commit message:
        HADOOP-7629. Allow immutable FsPermission objects to be used
 as IPC parameters. Contributed by Todd Lipcon.

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/hadoop/common/trunk@1170451 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68  

